  "worked_solution": "First, we find the lowest and highest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The lowest $y$-value is $1.$ This occurs at the point $(-2,1).$\n\n- The highest $y$-value is $5.$ This occurs at the point $(2,5).$\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $1$ and $5,$ including both $1$ and $5.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $1\\le y\\le 5,$ which can also be written as  $1\\le f(x)\\le 5.$",
